<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-9663] MVCC: Data node failure can cause TX hanging.</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9663</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Next test hangs due to a bug:&lt;br/&gt;
CacheMvccTransactionsTest.testPutAllGetAll_ClientServer_Backups1_Restart_Scan&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Possibly, it is caused with a race in MvccTracker and can be partially fixed in&#160;&lt;a href=&quot;#1&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;noopener&quot;&gt;1&lt;/a&gt;&#160;or&#160;&lt;br/&gt;
we have a bug in TX mapping in enlist phase on unstable topology.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;I&apos;ve tried to avoid races in Tracker and see TX hanged awaiting PME that version has just been completed. This need to be investigated.&lt;br/&gt;
&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;1&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&#160;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9428&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow&quot;&gt;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-9428&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
